        {
          "expected_id": "n01-f1",
          "location": "src/logger.rs:32-35",
          "issue_type": "Correctness",
          "description": "The guard now compares the number of buffered entries against `config.max_entries`, but the ring does not hold `max_entries` entries. `RingBuffer::with_capacity` clamps its request to `HARD_CAP` (64), so for any configuration above 64 the ring fills at 64 and `len()` can never reach `max_entries`. The guard therefore never fires: `append` keeps returning `Ok`, `RingBuffer::push` silently overwrites the oldest entry, and the documented contract that the logger reports `LogError::Full` rather than discarding anything is broken. `rejected()` also stays at zero, so the loss is invisible to operators. The replaced `buffer.is_full()` asked the ring about its own real capacity and was correct at any configured value."
        }
      ],
